<header><p class="enc-kicker">Institution</p><h1 class="enc-title">Viceroy of Kush</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/viceroy-of-india">Viceroy</a> of Kush, also called the King's Son of Kush, was the official who governed <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nubia">Nubia</a> on behalf of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pharaoh">pharaoh</a> during <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/egypt">Egypt</a>'s <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/new-kingdom-of-egypt">New Kingdom</a>. The Egyptian Empire New Kingdom profile describes the office as a semi-autonomous imperial sub-administration. It oversaw the region's gold production, tribute and garrisons.</p></div>
